{
  "ticket": "to be minted at cast",
  "status": "DRAFT shaped plan by akienyoga9i_cc_0, 2026-11-14, split per the orchestrator's ruling (c), for akienasus to cast. Not cast; no record written. Ticket A of two; B is a-build-that-removes-a-charter-repoints-the-tickets-it-owns.shaped-plan.json, with A as its parent.",
  "title": "every ticket's owning_intention names a charter that stands",
  "node_class": "code-seam",
  "task_or_ticket": "task",
  "owning_intention": "cairn/tools/ticket_inspector/intention+why.json",
  "intention": "Every ticket's owning_intention either names an existing charter, which cross.charter_dir resolves under one of the two roots, or reads 'none because <path> was retired by ticket <id> (<commit>, <date>)'. The 32 dead owners whose component moved are repointed to where it went, and the 4 dead watchme paths with a measured successor are repointed too. The 12 closed tickets whose component was deleted are marked retired, with the original path kept inside the sentence. The one open ticket whose component was deleted (5a4ec289bf15) has its watch retired with what it watched, and its cursor is moved through the door with that citation. All of it goes through the artifact door, one field per write. The tooth that stops the next rename from doing this again is ticket B.",
  "why": "Measured 2026-11-14. The census script census_dead_paths.py read every plan and state file under CairnCommons/tickets, 995 plans in all. 45 tickets name an owning_intention that resolves under neither root, so a reader that resolves the owner throws ValueError (cross.charter_dir:51, clearance/gate.py:67). The orchestrator's lacks census hit this, and 7ea5 failed on the same error earlier. There are three causes, all measured. (a) f942a413f26d (60e1dd170, 2026-11-13) rewrote the inference proxy's charter enough that git records a delete plus an add, not a rename, and the ticket carries no forwarding order. So build_inspector's successor door (derived_successor / continued_successor) returns nothing for all 25 inference_domain owners. (b) Earlier moves did leave a git rename record, and the successor door does answer them (8 of 8 agree with the census). But the owning_intention readers resolve the literal path only, so the answer goes unread. (c) Six retirements on 2026-11-08 deleted charters that 13 tickets still name. Nothing in the crossing checks whether a deleted charter is still somebody's owner. ticket_inspector.owning_intention_resolves sees all 45, but it runs only inside the advisory watch probe the_corpus_gets_cleaner.",
  "traces_to": "Law 7 (a record of truth stays readable: a dead pointer is an error that looks like data), Law 5 (a ticket and its component may not contradict about where the component is), Law 6 (the cursor moves only through the owner's gate, never by hand).",
  "sequencing": "A LANDS AFTER 049249b867ec (write_state merges onto the standing state). D1's 4 watchme writes and D5 are state-file writes; before 0492, a partial state write replaces the whole file, which is the 4bf3b3cb failure that wiped four tickets' .state.json.",
  "falsifier": {
    "clauses": [
      {
        "n": 1,
        "claim": "after the build, every plan under CairnCommons/tickets has an owning_intention that cross.charter_dir resolves under the cairn or commons root, or that starts 'none because' and names the retiring ticket id; the census reads 0 dead owners where it read 45"
      },
      {
        "n": 2,
        "claim": "each owner write (44) and watchme write (4) changed exactly one field of one file: a field-level diff, every other key byte for byte the same, made through the artifact door and journaled. The state-field writes keep every standing state field"
      },
      {
        "n": 3,
        "claim": "5a4ec289bf15's watchme.probe reads 'none because cairn/machines/counting_block/probes/raise_rate_falls.py was retired by ticket 6935a4a71f93 (f2b0d8105, 2026-11-08)', its owning_intention reads the same form for its charter, and its cursor has left WATCHME through the transitions door with a why citing 6935a4a71f93. If the door refuses the move, nothing is written by hand: the refusal is recorded verbatim and sent to the orchestrator as a finding, and this clause reads that the refusal stands on record"
      }
    ]
  },
  "decisions": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "text": "D1 REPOINT: for each row in measured.repoint and measured.watchme_repoint, the field is set to its 'to' through the artifact door (ticket_file.rewrite_ticket for plan fields, write_state for state fields), why 'owning_intention repointed: <from> moved to <to> (<moving ticket>)'. Refused, with nothing written, if 'to' does not exist at write time or the field no longer reads 'from'. Successors are measured, not guessed: 25 by the prefix inference_domain/ -> inferenceproxy/ with the target existing (f942's move); 6 by a unique basename, which git's rename record agrees with; 1 (c23cc599a107 orient) by git's rename record c262f05ab alone, because the basename has 2 candidates.",
      "writes_to": [
        "CairnCommons/tickets/ (the plan files in measured.repoint; the state files in measured.watchme_repoint)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "text": "D2 RETIRED OWNER: for each row in measured.retire, owning_intention becomes 'none because <from> was retired by ticket <retired_by> (<commit>, <on>)', which is the form ticket_inspector already honours. cross.charter_dir refuses it, and that is right: a component that no longer exists cannot take a crossing. hermes has no deleting commit in this repo's git log, so its sentence says 'retired before this repo's history (no deleting commit found)'. Only closed tickets are written here (PROVED, SUPERSEDED, RETIRED); the open one is D5.",
      "writes_to": [
        "CairnCommons/tickets/ (the plan files in measured.retire, except 5a4ec289bf15)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "text": "D3 5a4ec289bf15 (ruling (a), orchestrator 2026-11-14): the watch retires with what it watched. owning_intention and watchme.probe both get the D2 sentence, citing 6935a4a71f93, f2b0d8105 and 2026-11-08. The cursor then moves out of WATCHME through the transitions door (the cairn ticket verb that crosses or retires, never a hand edit of workflow_and_state), with why 'its watched component and probe were deleted by 6935a4a71f93 (f2b0d8105, 2026-11-08); the watch retires with what it watched'. The chart reads which target the door offers a WATCHME ticket (RETIRED or SUPERSEDED). A refusal is the finding, and it goes to the orchestrator.",
      "writes_to": [
        "CairnCommons/tickets/5a4ec289bf15-a-counting-learning-block-predicts-who-writes-what-from-the-artifact-journal.json",
